{"version":1,"reference":{"kind":"plan","namespace":"","artifact_type":"","name":"Pd95e593c"},"owner_reference":"#3151","content":"{\"plan_id\":\"Pd95e593c\",\"feature\":\"sam-task-file-language\",\"version\":\"1.0.0\",\"description\":\"\",\"goal\":\"Close the file-based SAM-task language loop by fixing the two structural sources that regenerate it (the ActiveTaskContext.task_file_path data contract and the AGENTS.md required-reading route to docs/TASK_FILE_FORMAT.md), then sweeping the ~46 prose files that the loop produced. Prose tasks are gated behind the complete structural tier so nothing regenerates the language mid-sweep.\",\"context\":\"# Plan context \\u2014 #3151\\n\\n## Invariant this plan enforces\\n\\nA SAM task is a backend record addressed as `P{id}/T{id}`. It is never read or written by a file operation \\u2014 EXCEPT inside the local-YAML `ContextBackend`/`TaskBackend`, where file storage is genuinely correct and must not be touched.\\n\\n## Why ordering is load-bearing, not tidiness\\n\\n`task_status_hook.py:_extract_plan_addr_from_path()` regexes `(P[0-9a-f]+)` out of `task_file_path`. That only ever worked because memory/github/beads fabricated paths that happened to embed the address in the filename. The moment T1+T2 land and `task_file_path` becomes `None` for those three backends, that regex silently returns `None` for every non-local session. T3 is therefore a functional-regression fix, not a cleanup \\u2014 and every prose task is gated behind the whole structural tier (T1-T6) because prose is the loop's OUTPUT: sweeping before the generators are dead means re-sweeping.\\n\\n## Anti-goals (do not touch)\\n\\n1. `local_context_backend.py`, `local_yaml.py`, `writers/yaml_writer.py`, `readers/*` and their tests \\u2014 the file vocabulary is correct there.\\n2. Plan-side sweep already closed by merged PRs #3159, #3161, #3137, #3156; `.claude/rules/large-file-write-strategy.md`.\\n3. File storage as a backend option \\u2014 only the SHARED session-context model's assumption that every backend has one.\\n4. Legacy-format migration code/tests: `migrate_tasks_to_github.py`, `test_cli_migrate_fallback.py`, `nonstandard_frontmatter_tasks.md`.\\n5. `graphify-out/*` \\u2014 generated artifacts.\\n6. `implementation_manager.py:1354-1371` \\u2014 its `task_file_path` is an UNRELATED CLI positional argument for the local-YAML-only `claim_task` command; it never reads `ActiveTaskContext`. Verify (T6), never rename.\\n7. `plugins/plugin-creator/{agents/refactor-executor.md, skills/start-refactor-task/SKILL.md, skills/implement-refactor/SKILL.md}` \\u2014 confirmed false positives; a different, genuinely file-based subsystem (`.plugin-creator/plans/tasks-refactor-{slug}.md`).\\n8. `research/README.md` and `research/insights/*.md` \\u2014 dated historical snapshots; do not rewrite research history.\\n\\n## Test-update policy\\n\\nTest fixtures asserting literal fabricated paths are folded into the task that breaks them, NOT deferred to a later task. No task in this plan may complete with CI red. Mapping: `sam_schema/tests/test_parent_issue_number_widening.py` -> T1; backend fixtures -> T2; `tests/test_task_status_hook.py`, `tests_backlog/test_task_status_hook_beads.py`, `tests/test_dh_paths_integration.py` -> T3.\\n\\n## Two distinct workflow-architecture-diagram files\\n\\nThey are NOT the same file. `plugins/development-harness/docs/workflow-architecture-diagram.md` (23K) is a dead-link repair target in T9. `.claude/docs/workflow-architecture-diagram.md` (17K) is a separate repo-root file with literal `task_file_path` JSON examples, handled in T11. Do not conflate.\\n\\n## Decision recorded: `docs/dh-backend-beads/comparison-research/*.md`\\n\\nINCLUDED in T11 (the Impact Radius correction left this to task decomposition). Rationale: unlike `research/insights/*`, these carry no date-stamp and are written in the present tense as descriptions of the CURRENT mechanism \\u2014 `04-dh-sam-system.md:680` is a field-definition table row that becomes factually wrong the moment T1 lands. Scope is deliberately minimal: correct the four factually-wrong lines (`04-dh-sam-system.md:310,666,680`, `07-skills-hooks-beads-integration.md:399`), do not rewrite the comparison's conclusions.\\n\\n## Paths\\n\\nAll code paths are relative to `plugins/development-harness/` unless prefixed with `.claude/` or `docs/dh-backend-beads/`, which are repo-root.\\n\\n## Sources\\n\\n- Architecture spec: `plan/architect-sam-task-file-language.md` (artifact type `architect`, item #3151)\\n- Discovery: `plan/feature-context-sam-task-file-language.md` (artifact type `feature-context`, item #3151)\\n- Impact Radius incl. the authoritative CORRECTION entry dated 2026-08-28: `backlog_view(selector=\\\"#3151\\\", navigate=\\\"7.1\\\")`\",\"acceptance_criteria\":\"\",\"issue\":\"3151\",\"tasks\":[{\"id\":\"T0\",\"title\":\"Baseline capture: record pre-change state of all eight structured acceptance criteria\",\"status\":\"complete\",\"agent\":\"dh:t0-baseline-capture\",\"dependencies\":[],\"blocked_by\":[],\"parallelize_with\":[],\"priority\":1,\"complexity\":\"low\",\"skills\":[\"python-engineering:python3-typing\",\"python-engineering:python3-testing\",\"python-engineering:modernpython\",\"plugin-creator:claude-plugins-reference-2026\"],\"created\":\"2026-08-28T13:50:09.333800+00:00\",\"started\":null,\"completed\":\"2026-08-28T14:23:03.293612+00:00\",\"last_activity\":null,\"body\":\"\",\"description\":\"Run each check-command in acceptance-criteria-structured and record its exit status and output verbatim. Non-zero exits are EXPECTED here (AC1-AC4 and AC8 are designed to fail at baseline) and are not failures of this task.\",\"objective\":\"Capture the T0 baseline for every criterion in the plan's acceptance-criteria-structured list so TN can prove the delta rather than assert it.\",\"requirements\":\"Run all eight check-commands. Record exit code plus first ~20 lines of output for each. Register the result as a t0