ressure at its source.\\n\\nThe class docstring at ~737-745 is separately and actively WRONG, not merely imprecise: it claims \\\"The SubagentStop hook reads this file directly from the filesystem\\\". That is true only for the local backend. The hook's PRIMARY retrieval path is the `sam_active_task(action=\\\"get\\\")` fastmcp call (`task_status_hook.py:331-370`); the file read is a fallback, and for memory/GitHub/beads no such file is ever written. A docstring on the fabricating field's own home model teaching the file model is the same defect species this whole plan exists to close, so it is in scope here, not deferred as polish.\",\"objective\":\"Stop `ActiveTaskContext` from requiring a filesystem path that three of four backends do not have, and stop its own docstring from teaching the file model.\",\"requirements\":\"1. Change the field to `task_file_path: str | None = Field(default=None, description=\\\"Absolute path to the plan YAML file containing this task. Populated only by the local-YAML ContextBackend; None for memory, GitHub, and beads.\\\")`.\\n2. Rewrite the `ActiveTaskContext` class docstring so it states the binding is identified by its `(plan, task)` address across ALL backends, and that persistence as `context_dir()/active-task-{session_id}.json` is a local-backend storage detail rather than a universal contract. Remove the claim that the SubagentStop hook reads the file directly.\\n3. Update `sam_schema/tests/test_parent_issue_number_widening.py`, which constructs `ActiveTaskContext` with a literal path fixture, so it no longer asserts a fabricated path is required.\",\"constraints\":\"Do NOT tighten `plan: str | None` or `task: str | None` to required. Both are already set unconditionally by every backend's `set_active_task`, but pre-existing on-disk `active-task-{session_id}.json` files written before those fields existed (crashed or stale sessions) would fail `model_validate` if they became required. That tightening is independently decidable and is out of scope. Do NOT introduce a `LocalActiveTaskContext` subtype \\u2014 the `ContextBackend` Protocol (`sam_schema/core/context_backend.py:52-67`) declares one return type for all four backends and every consumer is typed against it; a subtype forces a union or isinstance narrowing at every call site for a field with no cross-field invariant to protect. Touch no other model.\",\"expected_outputs\":\"Modified `sam_schema/core/models.py` and `sam_schema/tests/test_parent_issue_number_widening.py`.\",\"acceptance_criteria\":\"1. `task_file_path` is `str | None` with `default=None` and a description naming the local-YAML backend as its only populator. 2. The class docstring contains no claim that the SubagentStop hook reads the file from the filesystem, and names `(plan, task)` as the cross-backend identity. 3. `uv run pytest sam_schema/tests/test_parent_issue_number_widening.py -q` passes. 4. `uv run ty check` (or the project's configured type checker) reports no new errors.\",\"verification_steps\":\"CoVe \\u2014 answer each before declaring done:\\n1. Did I verify by reading `context_backend.py:52-67` that the Protocol return type is a bare `ActiveTaskContext`, confirming the optional-field decision over a subtype split? Quote the signature.\\n2. Did I confirm `plan` and `task` are still `str | None` and that I did NOT tighten them?\\n3. Does the new docstring make a claim I have verified in `task_status_hook.py`, rather than one I assumed? Cite the line range showing the fastmcp call is the primary path.\\n4. Did I check whether any OTHER model or serializer in `sam_schema/` assumes `task_file_path` is non-None? Run `grep -rn 'task_file_path' sam_schema/` and account for every hit.\",\"context_notes\":\"This is the root of the whole plan: every other structural task depends on this field being allowed to be absent. Do not expand scope into the backends (T2) or the hook (T3) \\u2014 they have their own tasks and their own tests.\",\"handoff\":\"T2 relies o